  "enhanced_information": "In a patient with hepatic cirrhosis and ascites who develops a pleural effusion with low LDH and protein ratios, the effusion is likely transudative, associated with the liver disease. Initial management should focus on the underlying liver condition while expanding the pleural fluid analysis to exclude other causes. Invasive procedures or empirical antibiotics are not recommended without further evidence of complications like infection or malignancy.",
